<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) / Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) RA–FGF8/Wnt mutual cross-inhibition bistable determination wavefront in vertebrate somitogenesis, gated by a Lewis (2003) delayed Her1/Hes7 clock lattice on 2D bilateral paraxial mesoderm strips — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring (L1-103) enumerates Governing Laws 1-5 with the Lean theorem names and the 9 references; Sections 3b-3d carry per-function docstrings citing Lewis (2003) equations and figures and Vermot & Pourquié (2005); `morphoeval/math_kg_loops/baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.yaml` registers 6 equations with refreshed code loci and Lean loci (L1-205). Deduction: Panel B is rendered on a 1500 um domain while the measurements use the 1000 um default (L1610-1616), a disclosed but non-obvious split." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py L1610–L1616: Panel B uses L_psm_um = 1500 to avoid clipping the VAD front; measurements keep the 1000 um default <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py#L1610-L1616>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) / Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) RA–FGF8/Wnt mutual cross-inhibition bistable determination wavefront in vertebrate somitogenesis, gated by a Lewis (2003) delayed Her1/Hes7 clock lattice on 2D bilateral paraxial mesoderm strips — Model fidelity to source: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Keeps the faithful Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) cross-inhibition + CYP26A1 PDE system and hysteresis S-curve (L191-296, L297-435) and adds the two mechanisms the v2 audit asked for with the papers' own equations: Lewis (2003) Eqs. 1-3 delayed autoinhibition DDE per PSM cell with published rate constants, delayed saturating Notch-Delta input and Lewis's own random gene-release initial condition (L526-816; T_osc = 92.0 min vs 90 observed; in-phase at T_N = T_osc, anti-phase at T_osc/2 as in Lewis Fig. 4C-D), and the 2D bilateral reaction-diffusion extension with the Vermot & Pourquié RA-buffering law (L819-1030; VAD offset matches the analytic law to < 1 um). Score moves 94 -> 93 because the coupling exposed a structural defect: clock-gated arrest yields irregular cohorts (segment-length CV 0.69, L799, vs ~0.05 in chick) and the 2D WT front sits at 509 um vs 571 um in 1D because the neural-tube factor (L866, L903) perturbs the strips transversely; the DeltaC branch is a reduced readout (L452-453, L636). 6 Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) cover Laws 1-6." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py L799–L802: segment_length_cv = 0.69 and saltatory_index are reported honestly; the CV exposes irregular cohort sizes (new remediation item) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py#L799-L802>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-model-fidelity-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-model-fidelity-7> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) / Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) RA–FGF8/Wnt mutual cross-inhibition bistable determination wavefront in vertebrate somitogenesis, gated by a Lewis (2003) delayed Her1/Hes7 clock lattice on 2D bilateral paraxial mesoderm strips — Morphometric validation: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1375-1595) now yields 11 reference-anchored measurements (5 carried + 6 new): T_osc = 92.0 min vs 90 min (Palmeirim 1997), S = v_g*T_osc = 153.3 um vs 150 um, Notch nearest-neighbour coherence 0.84 vs 0.03 ablated, competence window 2.81 segments vs the >= 1 Goldbeter Fig. 10 criterion, 2D VAD LR offset 149.8 um vs 150 um analytic / one somite, and N_LR = 1.00 vs 1.0 observed with 4/4 sides correct (mean abs error 0.012 somites). Deduction: the cohort-level segment length (mean 127 um, SD 88 um over 13 core cohorts) is far noisier than the observed 150 +/- 8 um, so the saltatory-arrest metric validates the mechanism qualitatively, not the segment-size distribution; the WT 2D offset differs by grid (6.3 vs 6.5 um)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py L715–L760: Cohort detection by a 0.5*T consecutive-cell arrest-time threshold; yields irregular cohort extents (SD 88 um) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py#L715-L760>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-2d-bilateral-paraxial-strip-left-right-determination-front-offset-under-vad>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-chick-psm-bistable-determination-front-position-x-front-and-10-90-switch-width>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-chick-vertebrate-embryo-sem-specimen-bilateral-somite-spacing-s-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-clock-derived-somite-length-s-v-g-t-osc-from-the-delayed-her1-hes7-oscillator>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-goldbeter-baker-5-regime-ra-fgf-perturbation-somite-length-pearson-correlation-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-goldbeter-et-al-2007-bistability-competence-window-width-in-segments>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-lewis-2003-delayed-her1-hes7-autoinhibition-segmentation-clock-period-t-osc>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-notch-delta-nearest-neighbour-phase-coherence-r-at-the-determination-front>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-ra-fgf8-wnt-saddle-node-bistable-hysteresis-window-width-delta-m-m-2-m-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-vermot-pourquie-2005-left-right-somite-count-difference-n-lr-across-4-regimes>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-measurement-vitamin-a-deficiency-vad-anterior-wavefront-shift-compressed-somite-length-s-vad>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) / Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) RA–FGF8/Wnt mutual cross-inhibition bistable determination wavefront in vertebrate somitogenesis, gated by a Lewis (2003) delayed Her1/Hes7 clock lattice on 2D bilateral paraxial mesoderm strips — MorphoEval overall 92.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 post-remediation evaluation of `2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py` (92.0/100, up from 91.3/100 in Pass 2). Both v2 remediation items are closed: (1) the Goldbeter-Pourquié bistable switch is now gated by a Lewis (2003) delayed Her1/Hes7 autoinhibition oscillator lattice with delayed saturating Notch-Delta coupling (T_osc = 92.0 min vs 90 min observed, Lewis closed form 86.0 min; clock-derived S = 153.3 um vs 150 um; competence window 2.81 segments >= 1 as Goldbeter Fig. 10 requires; Notch ablation collapses nearest-neighbour coherence 0.84 -> 0.03 and the saltatory index 0.87 -> 0.42, cohorts 127 um vs 47 um; T_N = T_osc/2 anti-phase), and (2) the 1D PSM is extended to 2D bilateral paraxial strips with an RA-buffered lateralizing bias (WT offset 0.04 somite, VAD 1.00 somite left-delayed, situs inversus / Raldh2-/- right-delayed; 4/4 regimes side-correct, max error 0.04 somites). The remediation also exposed the next layer of defects, carried below: the saltatory cohorts are irregular (segment-length CV 0.69 vs ~0.05 observed), the 2D wild-type front (509 um) does not coincide with the 1D front (571 um) because of the transverse neural-tube coupling, b_LR is a fitted constant, the 1D solver's 1000 um domain clips the VAD front, and the DeltaC pathway is reduced to a transcript readout. 11 reference-anchored measurements, 7-section self-test, 6 Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys). Overall 92.0/100 (faithfulness 91.7, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 94, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py at d58a084, image/png, 1793783 B, 2352×2016 px, artifact_sha256 ce04ae4bd568fab038e1731acc826d8aade9d36fef83013221614779e63441e8 (sha256 ce04ae4bd568fab038e1731acc826d8aade9d36fef83013221614779e63441e8), spec_fingerprint 8dd375129916874341f9ce3cd615881707510415d2e6ec1d5f2914264a78a000. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8dd375129916874341f9ce3cd615881707510415d2e6ec1d5f2914264a78a000; artifact_sha256: ce04ae4bd568fab038e1731acc826d8aade9d36fef83013221614779e63441e8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/chick_ra_fgf_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront_reference.json=42c6196ddd32cee9..., datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/fgf_wnt_clock_lr_reference.json=16deab8565d154cb..., datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/scout_manifest.json=783faa9ee6b3db0c...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Cell / Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508 mutual cross-inhibition + CYP26A1 RA-degradation PDEs producing an S-shaped hysteresis curve [M_1, M_2], an all-or-none determination front switch, and (Fig. 10) a bistability window that must span at least one segment so the clock can time the arrest | Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) J. Theor. Biol. 239:413-429 & Diez del Corral et al. (2003) Neuron 40:65-79 opposing Vitamin A Deficiency (VAD) anterior front shift vs exogenous RA / SU5402 posterior front shift | Lewis (2003) Curr. Biol. 13:1398-1408 delayed autoinhibition her1/her7 oscillator (Eqs. 1-3, period ~ 2(T_m + T_p + 1/b + 1/c)), Notch-Delta synchronisation of adjacent cells and anti-phase locking at half-period coupling delay (Fig. 4); Palmeirim et al. (1997) Cell 91:639-648 90-min chick c-hairy1 period | Vermot & Pourquie (2005) Nature 435:215-220 and Vermot et al. (2005) Science 308:563-566: RA buffers a lateralizing bias so WT somites form bilaterally in synchrony, whereas VAD / disulfiram chick (left delayed) and Raldh2-/- mouse (right delayed) show a one-somite left-right desynchronisation that reverses under situs inversus; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical inverse hysteresis S-curve M(F) solver extracting lower saddle-node M_1 = 1.0254 nM and upper saddle-node M_2 = 3.3038 nM (Delta_M = 2.2784 nM) | 1D coupled RA-FGF8/Wnt reaction-diffusion PDE solver along the 1000 um chick PSM demonstrating 22.2x sharpening of the determination front (Delta_x_front = 16.22 um vs lambda_M = 360.67 um) at x_front = 571.46 um | 150-cell delayed Her1/Hes7 DDE lattice with delayed saturating Notch-Delta input, advected at v_g through the competence window [149.4, 571.4] um; cells arrest only at a Her protein peak -> saltatory cohort arrest (T_osc = 92.0 min, S = v_g*T_osc = 153.3 um, nearest-neighbour coherence 0.84 vs 0.03 Notch-ablated, saltatory index 0.87 vs 0.42) | 2D (x, y) RA-FGF8/Wnt reaction-diffusion solve on left strip + neural tube + right strip (1500 x 500 um) with RA-buffered lateralizing bias; WT Delta_x_LR = 6.3 um (0.04 somite), VAD 149.8 um (1.00 somite, left delayed), situs inversus and Raldh2-/- mouse right delayed; v_sc buffering sweep monotone | 5-regime somite perturbation evaluator (Pearson r = 0.9999, RMSE = 0.81 um) plus bilateral dorsal somite row segmentation on chick_ra_fgf_somites_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing); transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior chick presomitic mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows; the 2D bilateral strip geometry (strip half-width 250 um, neural tube half-width 80 um) is derived from the specimen's two somite-row pixel offsets | Lewis (2003) zebrafish her1 rate constants (a, b, c, k, p_0) reused with chick-scale transcription delay T_m = 31.5 min to reach the 90-min chick period; does_not_claim: Full 3D mesenchymal-to-epithelial somite rosette mechanics | Explicit deltaC mRNA/protein kinetics: Notch-Delta coupling is a delayed saturating readout of neighbour her1 transcript with K_D = k/(2c) (Lewis publishes no numeric value) | A molecular origin for the lateralizing bias b_LR = 0.727: it is a calibrated free parameter fitted to the one-somite VAD lag, buffered by anterior RA through a Hill law." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2D wild-type front x = 509.5 um (`solve_bilateral_2d_ra_fgf`, L837-1030) vs 571.5 um in 1D: the neural-tube factor 0.3 (L866, L903) couples transversely into the strips. Calibrate neural-tube boundary conditions / transverse diffusion so the strip midline front reproduces the 1D front, and make the WT offset grid-independent (6.3 um at nx=181 vs 6.5 um at nx=201).",
        "remediation needed: Notch-Delta coupling is a delayed saturating readout of neighbour her1 transcript with K_D = k/(2c) = 71.74 (L452-453, L636). Implement Lewis (2003) explicit deltaC mRNA/protein equations and derive the coupling constant from them.",
        "remediation needed: Saltatory cohorts are irregular: segment_length_cv = 0.69 (`simulate_delayed_her_clock_lattice`, L799) vs ~0.05 observed (150 +/- 8 um), and cohort boundaries come from a 0.5*T consecutive-cell arrest-time threshold (L715-760). Add a Mesp2/Tbx6 boundary-determination step or phase-wave prepattern so each clock cycle arrests a regular ~12-cell cohort.",
        "remediation needed: Unify domain length: the 1D solver default L_psm_um = 1000 (L298) clips the VAD front at x = 1000 um, so Panel B had to use 1500 um (L1610-1616) while measurements keep 1000 um. Use one domain for solver, measurements and figure.",
        "remediation needed: Wire --v-sc/--vg/--Tc/--seed (and the new Pass 3 flags) into the default figure/GIF render (`main`, L2157-2221); currently only --print-pass3 consumes them.",
        "remediation needed: b_LR = 0.727, K_buf = 1.0 nM, h_buf = 4 (`ra_lr_buffering_factor`, L819-836; default in L839) are fitted to the one-somite VAD lag. Derive b_eff from a Nodal/Pitx2 or left-right fgf8 expression asymmetry readout with a cited magnitude." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) / Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) RA–FGF8/Wnt mutual cross-inhibition bistable determination wavefront in vertebrate somitogenesis, gated by a Lewis (2003) delayed Her1/Hes7 clock lattice on 2D bilateral paraxial mesoderm strips — Parameter expressivity: 94/100" ;
