    dct:description "Beyond the 5 RA/FGF regimes, Pass 3 adds a clock-delay sweep against Lewis's closed form (`sweep_clock_delay`, L1032-1061), a Notch-coupling ablation (`ablate_notch_coupling`, L1063-1088), an RA-buffering sweep across v_sc (`sweep_lr_buffering`, L1090-1116, monotone in the self-test) and a 4-regime left-right evaluator including situs inversus and the Raldh2-/- mouse (`evaluate_lr_regimes`, L1118-1164). New CLI flags --clock-delay, --notch-delay, --notch-coupling, --lr-bias, --situs and --print-pass3 (L2168-2213) drive the new solvers and print a JSON summary. Deduction: the pre-existing --v-sc/--vg/--Tc/--seed flags are consumed only by --print-pass3; the default figure/GIF render still ignores them (L2213-2218)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py L2157–L2221: CLI: six new Pass 3 flags and --print-pass3 JSON summary; --v-sc/--vg/--Tc/--seed not wired into the default render <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py#L2157-L2221>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-parameter-expressivity-1>,
